   "html_text": "Against Wheeler & Fischer (2012), Scarantino (2013) and Scarantino & Clay (2015) defend the explanatory value of the functional reference framework. They argue that the problem is not with the framework itself, but only with the existing characterisation of functional reference. They point out that while context-independence and stimulus-specificity don’t always apply to cases of animal communication, they don’t apply to cases of human linguistic reference, either. Examples of this include index",
